REFERENCE","values":["ScheduleY"]},{"name":"dutchNameLong","type":"STRING","values":["Structure course non-western languages (Quechua) TEN"]},{"name":"englishNameLong","type":"STRING","values":["Structure course non-western languages (Quechua) TEN"]},{"name":"schedulePrint","subType":"yesNoReference","type":"REFERENCE","values":["Y"]},{"name":"gradingScale","subType":"gradingScaleRef","type":"REFERENCE","values":["GRD"]},{"name":"dutchNameShort","type":"STRING","values":["Struct.non west. lang TEN"]}],"year":{"code":"2026-2027","id":"2261","names":[{"language":"EN","value":"2026-2027"},{"language":"NL","value":"2026-2027"}],"uid":"07254806-916f-4cca-82a0-2e69a4a95e9f"}},"required":true,"values":[{"name":"evaluate","subType":"yesNoReference","type":"REFERENCE","values":["Y"]}],"weighting":1.00}],"capacity":{"optimum":35.00},"code":"5511KEBE1Y","credits":{"maximum":5.00,"minimum":5.00,"optimum":5.00},"descriptions":[{"language":"EN","text":"We will study the Andean language Quechua as an example of a non-western language. Quechua was the *lingua franca* of the Inca Empire and is still spoken by millions of people today. The language is spoken in six South American countries: Colombia, Ecuador, Peru, Bolivia, Chile, and Argentina.\n\nIn contrast to many western languages, Quechua expresses properties such as transitions (marking of both the subject and object on the verb), a four person system, switch reference in adverbial subordination, and evidentiality (the grammatical marking of information source). Another interesting property of the language is that it shows little irregularity.\n\nThe course will focus on the Ayacucho variety of the language family spoken in Peru. The main goal is to provide an overview of the phonology, morphology and syntax of this Quechua variety. Translation, glossing, and formulation exercises will be used in order to convey insights into the de grammar of the language. Through the course materials students will obtain insight into the cultural and sociolinguistic situation of the Andes.","type":{"code":"CO","id":"CO","names":[{"language":"EN","value":"Description"},{"language":"NL","value":"Beschrijving"}],"uid":"9b0c3e97-ad09-42d7-a5bb-afdaf6f1877f"}},{"language":"EN","text":"Homework assignments and readings will be provided on [Brightspace](https://brightspace.leidenuniv.nl/)","type":{"code":"LI","id":"LI","names":[{"language":"EN","value":"Reading list"},{"language":"NL","value":"Literatuurlijst"}],"uid":"fbd93a9e-ca99-4bcc-807f-39235bb6000b"}},{"language":"EN","text":"### Assessment\n\nMidterm examination with short open questions: 25%\nFinal examination with short open questions: 75%\n\nPresence and active participation in this course are mandatory. Students can be excluded from the course or obtain a lower grade if they do not meet these requirements.\n\n### Weighing\n\nThe final mark for the course is established by determining the weighted average.\n\n### ","type":{"code":"TP","id":"TP","names":[{"language":"EN","value":"Assessment method"},{"language":"NL","value":"Toetsing en weging"}],"uid":"687f9ba4-4330-4ab9-8536-be9ebd2c58c5"}},{"language":"EN","text":"Enrolment through MyStudyMap (button in upper right corner) is mandatory. General information about course and exam enrolment is available on the website https://www.student.universiteitleiden.nl/en/your-study-programme/courses-and-exams/enrolment/leiden-university","type":{"code":"ENR","id":"ENR","names":[{"language":"EN","value":"Registration"},{"language":"NL","value":"Inschrijven"}],"uid":"a77a2043-b0a9-450d-b780-1e90a4d3290c"}},{"language":"EN","text":"By the end of this course; students will be able to:\n\n* analyze the basic grammatical structures of Quechua;\n* provide interlinear glosses for brief Quechua texts;\n* provide interpretations of Quechua sentences based on the grammatical structures in the language;\n* describe the cultural and sociolinguistic situation of the Andes.","type":{"code":"LO","id":"LO","names":[{"language":"EN","value":"Course objectives"},{"language":"NL","value":"Leerdoelen"}],"uid":"b54eb210-96e8-490d-aadb-a70571a665d9"}},{"language":"EN","text":"None, but having taken the course Talen van de wereld / Languages of the World will be helpful.","type":{"code":"AR","id":"AR","names":[{"language":"EN","value":"Admission requirements"},{"language":"NL","value":"Toegangseisen"}],"uid":"2c481598-5834-4422-a338-1eb346d6f52c"}},{"language":"EN","text":"For substantive questions, contact the lecturer(s) (listed in the right information bar).  For questions about enrolment, admission, etc., contact the Education Administration Office: osz-oa-reuvensplaats@hum.leidenuniv.nl","type":{"code":"CG","id":"CG","names":[{"language":"EN","value":"Contact"},{"language":"NL","value":"Contact"}],"uid":"35f7e88a-830a-4877-b467-86a700954d19"}},{"language":"EN","text":"Seminar","type":{"code":"WV","id":"WV","names":[{"language":"EN","value":"Teaching method"},{"language":"NL","value":"Onderwijsvorm"}],"uid":"26f0e596-e48d-46ff-8c8b-9b9688699943"}},{"language":"EN","text":"The timetables are available through My Timetable (see the button in the upper right corner).","type":{"code":"SC","id":"SC","names":[{"language":"EN","value":"Schedule"},{"language":"NL","value":"Rooster"}],"uid":"939373d2-217d-4dde-9c37-6f6101f1ab75"}},{"language":"EN","text":"### Resit\n\nIf the weighted average is insufficient (below 5,5), students can take a resit (100%).\n\n### Exam review\n\nHow and when an exam review will take place will be disclosed together with the publication of the exam results at the latest. If a student requests a review within 30 days after publication of the exam results, an exam review will have to be organized.","type":{"code":"RRD","id":"RRD","names":[{"language":"EN","value":"Resit, review & feedback"},{"language":"NL","value":"Herkansing, inzage & nabespreking"}],"uid":"ef7be178-91d7-4f56-a40b-891976f3af1c"}}],"faculty":{"code":"FGW","id":"FGW","names":[{"language":"EN","value":"Humanities"},{"language":"NL","value":"Geesteswetenschappen"}],"uid":"28c8aabb-f896-444f-895c-63ef88ba9307"},"id":"236455","key":108750,"methods":[{"method":{"category":"T","code":"5511KEBE1H","contactHours":26.00,"id":"236458","key":126385,"module":{"code":"5511KEBE1Y","id":"236455","names":[{"language":"EN","value":"Structure course non-western language (Quechua)"},{"language":"NL","value":"Structure course non-western language (Quechua)"}],"uid":"89e35ecb-9465-4164-9509-f48ad14d5705"},"names":[{"language":"EN","value":"Structure course non-western language (Quechua) LEC"},{"language":"NL","value":"Structure course non-western language (Quechua) LEC"}],"type":"LEC","typeAbbreviation":"LEC","uid":"e4bb5f04-c996-4e80-a930-8808cd9bc809","values":[{"name":"studiegidsnummerY","type":"STRING","values":["5511KEBE1Y"]},{"name":"numberOfGroups","values":["1"]},{"name":"examDateFlag","subType":"yesNoReference","type":"REFERENCE","values":["N"]},{"name":"dutchNameLong","type":"STRING","values":["Structure course non-western language (Quechua)"]},{"name":"dynClassData","subType":"dynamicClassDataRef","type":"REFERENCE","values":["LEI5"]},{"name":"dutchNameshort","type":"STRING","values":["Struct.non west. lang LEC"]},{"name":"Werkvorm","type":"STRING","values":["LEC"]},{"name":"englishNameShort","type":"STRING","values":["Struct.non west. lang LEC"]},{"name":"englishNameLong","type":"STRING","values":["Structure course non-western language (Quechua)"]},{"name":"schedulePrint","subType":"yesNoReference","type":"REFERENCE","values":["Y"]},{"name":"gradingScale","subType":"gradingScaleRef","type":"REFERENCE","values":["ZB"]}],"year":{"code":"2026-2027","id":"2261","names":[{"language":"EN","value":"2026-2027"},{"language":"NL","value":"2026-2027"}],"uid":"07254806-916f-4cca-82a0-2e69a4a95e9f"}},"required":false}],"names":[{"language":"EN","value":"Structure course non-western language (Quechua)"},{"language":"NL","value":"Structure course non-western language (Quechua)"}],"offerin